    "body": "The differential equation $y^{\\prime \\prime}+(\\tan x) y^{\\prime}=0$ has two linearly independent solutions $y_{1}(x)=\\sin x$ and $y_{2}(x)=1$. If we use the method of Variation of Parameters to find a particular solution $y_{p}(x)=u_{1}(x) y_{1}(x)+u_{2}(x) y_{2}(x)$ for the corresponding nonhomogeneous equation\n\n\n\n\\[\ny^{\\prime \\prime}+(\\tan x) y^{\\prime}=\\cos ^{2} x\n\\]\n\nthen which of the following is a possible function $u_{1}(x)$ ?",
